From 52b7802bbbfba304b31cbbe8319de5c0545cdc0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:24:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] arm64: dts: rockchip: P25T: front camera DTB variant

New DTB rk3566-teclast-p25t-front.dtb: the base DT with the front
camera instead of the rear one (one CSI-2 host, one camera at a time).
GC02M2 on i2c2 at 0x10, reset GPIO4_B0 (active high), powerdown GPIO4_B3
(active low), same MCLK, power domain and supplies as the rear GC5035, 1
data lane on the D-PHY's lanes 2-3 (rockchip,split-lanes-2-3). The rear
sensor node is disabled and its port removed. Values from the stock
Android device tree.

The sensor is mounted turned by 180 degrees (without flips a picture
comes out upside down and mirrored; with both sensor flips it is
upright), described with rotation = <180> so that applications
(libcamera) turn on both flips.

Use it in place of rk3566-teclast-p25t.dtb to get the front camera; the
base DTB is unchanged.

P25T tests: p25t-sway tests/ 07-10 (by hand), 11, 20-21.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0156c5MfQpFxaYWNNLMrcym9
